# The delivery gate's checks, pinned against makesensedigital/engineering-handbook@v3.7.1.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `test-gate.mjs` — the gate's own two-direction test — cannot run in a
# repository that adopted the standard after its code existed: it builds its known-good fixture by
# copying the repository root and editing the TEMPLATE's placeholders out of it. So the claim that
# these checks are known to work rests on them matching the release where that test passes. This
# file turns that claim from an assertion into something the gate verifies on every run.
#
# FIVE OF THE SEVEN ARE BYTE-IDENTICAL TO v3.7.1. Two are not, and pretending otherwise is exactly
# the kind of thing this file exists to prevent:
#
#   lib.mjs — ONE LINE ADDED to `walk()`'s default skip list: `.gate-baseline.json`. Without it the
#   ratchet's own baseline is scanned as site content, its `check|file` keys are read as file
#   references, and each run manufactures a new finding whose baseline key is longer than the last.
#   It does not converge. engineering-handbook#54.
#
#   check-assets.mjs — ONE TOKEN ADDED to the reference scan's extension list: `css`. A stylesheet
#   is the most common place to reference a font or a background image, and it was the one file
#   type the scan did not read — ten self-hosted woff2 files, correctly referenced from
#   `assets/fonts.css`, were all reported as orphans. engineering-handbook#59.
#
# Both were found by running the gate rather than by reading it, and both are carried by debt #5.
#
# Editing ANY of these makes this check fail, which is the intended behaviour: at that moment the
# upstream test no longer covers it, and the correct next step is to vendor the pristine template
# into `scripts/fixtures/landing/` and make `test-gate.mjs` run for real. See debt #5.
